WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.571
Which sets of 2, 3, 6 and 7 add to 7?

00:04.571 --> 00:14.700
Trying every branch blindly means 28 nodes, most of them dead ends that overshoot.

00:15.000 --> 00:22.937
Try one number at a time and carry what is left.

00:22.937 --> 00:31.700
Each choice narrows the question to a smaller target.

00:32.000 --> 00:40.381
2, 2, 2 leaves only 1, and 2 is already too big, so that branch is cut.

00:40.381 --> 00:47.700
Back up: 2, 2 then 3 reaches exactly 7, so [2, 2, 3] is saved.

00:48.000 --> 00:57.157
Trying every branch is exponential, but each cut prunes a whole subtree.

00:57.157 --> 00:59.700
That’s backtracking.
